{"task_id": "Mbpp/11", "solution": "def remove_Occ(s: str, ch: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Removes the first and last occurrence of a given character from the string.\n    If the character appears only once, it is removed. If it does not appear, the string is returned unchanged.\n    \"\"\"\n    first_idx = s.find(ch)\n\n    if first_idx == -1:\n        return s\n\n    last_idx = s.rfind(ch)\n\n    if first_idx == last_idx:\n        # Only one occurrence\n        return s[:first_idx] + s[first_idx+1:]\n    else:\n        # Remove last occurrence first to preserve the index of the first occurrence\n        s_after_last_removed = s[:last_idx] + s[last_idx+1:]\n        # Remove first occurrence from the new string\n        return s_after_last_removed[:first_idx] + s_after_last_removed[first_idx+1:]"}
