{"task_id": "Mbpp/6", "solution": "def differ_At_One_Bit_Pos(a: int, b: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if two integers differ at exactly one bit position.\"\"\"\n\n    def _xor_numbers(val1: int, val2: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Computes the bitwise XOR of two integers.\"\"\"\n        return val1 ^ val2\n\n    def _popcount_bits(n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Counts the number of set bits (1s) in an integer.\"\"\"\n        # Uses int.bit_count() (Python 3.8+), as specified by design context.\n        return n.bit_count()\n\n    xor_result = _xor_numbers(a, b)\n    num_differing_bits = _popcount_bits(xor_result)\n\n    return num_differing_bits == 1"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/12", "solution": "def sort_matrix(matrix):\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a matrix in ascending order based on the sum of its rows.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Create a list of tuples, where each tuple contains (sum_of_row, original_row).\n    # Python's sorted() is stable, preserving the original order for rows with equal sums.\n    rows_with_sums = [(sum(row), row) for row in matrix]\n\n    # Sort the list of tuples based on the sum of the row (the first element of the tuple).\n    sorted_rows_with_sums = sorted(rows_with_sums, key=lambda x: x[0])\n\n    # Extract just the original rows from the sorted list of tuples.\n    sorted_matrix = [row_tuple[1] for row_tuple in sorted_rows_with_sums]\n\n    return sorted_matrix"}
