{"task_id": "Mbpp/94", "solution": "from typing import Iterable, Sequence, Any\ndef index_minimum(items: Iterable[Sequence[Any]]) -> Any:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the first value of the tuple with the smallest second value.\n    Raises IndexMinimumError for empty input or invalid item format/comparisons.\n    \"\"\"\n    it = iter(items)\n\n    try:\n        first_item = next(it)\n    except StopIteration:\n        raise IndexMinimumError(\"Input must be a non-empty iterable of sequences\")\n\n    if not hasattr(first_item, '__len__') or len(first_item) < 2:\n        raise IndexMinimumError(\"Each item must be a sequence with at least 2 elements\")\n\n    best_first = first_item[0]\n    best_second = first_item[1]\n\n    for current_item in it:\n        if not hasattr(current_item, '__len__') or len(current_item) < 2:\n            raise IndexMinimumError(\"Each item must be a sequence with at least 2 elements\")\n\n        current_first = current_item[0]\n        current_second = current_item[1]\n\n        try:\n            if current_second < best_second:\n                best_first = current_first\n                best_second = current_second\n        except TypeError as e:\n            raise IndexMinimumError(f\"Cannot compare second elements: {e}\") from e\n\n    return best_first"}
