{"task_id": "Mbpp/103", "solution": "def eulerian_num(n: int, m: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the Eulerian number a(n, m) using dynamic programming.\n    Follows the recurrence a(n, m) = (m + 1) * a(n - 1, m) + (n - m) * a(n - 1, m - 1).\n    \"\"\"\n    # Handle base cases and out-of-bounds as per definition\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1 if m == 0 else 0\n    if m < 0 or m >= n:\n        return 0\n\n    # Initialize a DP table where dp[i][j] stores a(i, j)\n    # The table size is (n+1) x (n+1) to accommodate indices up to n.\n    dp = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n\n    # Set the fundamental base case\n    dp[0][0] = 1\n\n    # Fill the DP table iteratively\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        for j in range(i):  # j represents m, and m must be < i for non-zero values\n            term1 = (j + 1) * dp[i - 1][j]\n            term2 = 0\n            if j - 1 >= 0:  # a(n, m) is 0 for m < 0, so dp[i-1][-1] is 0\n                term2 = (i - j) * dp[i - 1][j - 1]\n\n            dp[i][j] = term1 + term2\n\n    return dp[n][m]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/99", "solution": "def decimal_to_binary(decimal: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Converts a non-negative decimal integer to its binary equivalent as a string.\n    The string will have no leading zeros, except for the number 0 itself.\n    \"\"\"\n    if decimal == 0:\n        return \"0\"\n    \n    # Using bitwise operations for conversion\n    bits = []\n    while decimal > 0:\n        bits.append('1' if (decimal & 1) else '0')\n        decimal >>= 1\n        \n    return ''.join(reversed(bits))"}
