{"task_id": "Mbpp/137", "solution": "def zero_count(arr: list[int]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the ratio of zeroes to non-zeroes in an array of integers.\n    If there are no non-zero elements, returns float('inf').\"\"\"\n    \n    zeros = 0\n    total = 0\n    for x in arr:\n        if x == 0:\n            zeros += 1\n        total += 1\n            \n    non_zeros = total - zeros\n    \n    if non_zeros == 0:\n        return float('inf')\n    \n    return float(zeros) / non_zeros"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/138", "solution": "def is_Sum_Of_Powers_Of_Two(n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if an integer can be represented as a sum of distinct powers 2^k where k > 0.\n    This means the number must be positive and its binary representation must not use the 2^0 bit (i.e., it must be even).\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 0:\n        return False\n    # If the least significant bit is set, it means 2^0 (which is 1) is part of the sum.\n    # We want to exclude 2^0, so the number must be even.\n    if (n & 1) == 1:\n        return False\n    return True"}
