{"task_id": "Mbpp/170", "solution": "from typing import Sequence, Union\nNumber = Union[int, float]\ndef sum_range_list(items: Sequence[Number], start: int, end: int) -> Number:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of numbers in a list within a specified inclusive range.\n    This function iterates through the specified slice without creating a new list, optimizing for O(1) memory.\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    total: Number = 0\n    all_integers_in_range = True\n\n    # Iterate from the start index to the end index, inclusive.\n    for i in range(start, end + 1):\n        value = items[i]\n        total += value\n        \n        # If any value processed in the range is a float, the final sum should be a float.\n        if not isinstance(value, int):\n            all_integers_in_range = False\n            \n    # If all items within the range were integers, return the sum as an integer.\n    # Otherwise, return the sum as a float (which it would naturally be if floats were added).\n    if all_integers_in_range:\n        return int(total)\n    else:\n        return total"}
