{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "def is_majority(arr, n, x):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if an element x is the majority element in a sorted array arr of length n.\n    (Majority element occurs more than n/2 times.)\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _first_occurrence(current_arr, target_x) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Finds the first (leftmost) occurrence of target_x in current_arr using binary search.\n        Returns its index or -1 if not found.\n        \"\"\"\n        lo, hi = 0, len(current_arr) - 1\n        result = -1\n        while lo <= hi:\n            mid = (lo + hi) // 2\n            if current_arr[mid] == target_x:\n                result = mid\n                hi = mid - 1\n            elif current_arr[mid] < target_x:\n                lo = mid + 1\n            else:\n                hi = mid - 1\n        return result\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return False\n\n    first_idx = _first_occurrence(arr, x)\n\n    # If x is not found in the array, it cannot be a majority element.\n    if first_idx == -1:\n        return False\n\n    # A majority element must occur more than n/2 times.\n    # If the first occurrence is at `first_idx`, then the element at `first_idx + n // 2`\n    # must also be `x` for `x` to be a majority element.\n    # This implies there are at least `n // 2 + 1` occurrences of `x`.\n    majority_check_idx = first_idx + n // 2\n\n    # Check if the calculated index is within the array bounds\n    # and if the element at that position is indeed x.\n    if majority_check_idx < n and arr[majority_check_idx] == x:\n        return True\n    else:\n        return False"}
