{"task_id": "Mbpp/244", "solution": "import math\ndef next_Perfect_Square(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the next perfect square strictly greater than a given number.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        # The smallest non-negative perfect square is 0. If n is negative,\n        # 0 is strictly greater than n.\n        return 0\n    \n    # Calculate the integer square root of n.\n    root = math.isqrt(n)\n    \n    # If root * root is already greater than n, then root * root is the answer.\n    # This might happen if n is just slightly less than a perfect square.\n    # Otherwise, we need the square of (root + 1).\n    if root * root > n:\n        return root * root\n    else:\n        return (root + 1) * (root + 1)"}
