{"task_id": "Mbpp/245", "solution": "def max_sum(sequence: list) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum sum of a bitonic subsequence for the given array.\n    A sequence is bitonic if it is first strictly increasing and then strictly decreasing.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(sequence)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # inc_sum[i] stores the maximum sum of a strictly increasing subsequence ending at sequence[i]\n    inc_sum = [0] * n\n    for i in range(n):\n        inc_sum[i] = sequence[i]\n        for j in range(i):\n            if sequence[j] < sequence[i] and inc_sum[j] + sequence[i] > inc_sum[i]:\n                inc_sum[i] = inc_sum[j] + sequence[i]\n\n    # dec_sum[i] stores the maximum sum of a strictly decreasing subsequence starting at sequence[i]\n    dec_sum = [0] * n\n    for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n        dec_sum[i] = sequence[i]\n        for j in range(n - 1, i, -1):\n            if sequence[j] < sequence[i] and dec_sum[j] + sequence[i] > dec_sum[i]:\n                dec_sum[i] = dec_sum[j] + sequence[i]\n\n    # Combine increasing and decreasing sums to find the maximum bitonic sum.\n    # For each element sequence[i] as a potential peak, the sum is inc_sum[i] + dec_sum[i] - sequence[i].\n    # We subtract sequence[i] because it's included in both inc_sum[i] and dec_sum[i].\n    max_bitonic_sum = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        current_bitonic_sum = inc_sum[i] + dec_sum[i] - sequence[i]\n        if current_bitonic_sum > max_bitonic_sum:\n            max_bitonic_sum = current_bitonic_sum\n\n    return max_bitonic_sum"}
