{"task_id": "Mbpp/259", "solution": "def maximize_elements(a, b):\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the element-wise maximum of two sequences of 2-element tuples.\n    It assumes inputs are valid and of equal length, returning a tuple of resulting tuples.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = []\n    for tuple_a, tuple_b in zip(a, b):\n        max_first_element = max(tuple_a[0], tuple_b[0])\n        max_second_element = max(tuple_a[1], tuple_b[1])\n        result.append((max_first_element, max_second_element))\n    return tuple(result)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/261", "solution": "def division_elements(tuple_a, tuple_b):\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs element-wise division of two tuples, returning integer results if exact, else float.\n    Assumes valid, numeric inputs and no division by zero based on the design context.\n    \"\"\"\n    results = []\n    for num, den in zip(tuple_a, tuple_b):\n        raw_result = num / den\n        if float(raw_result).is_integer():\n            results.append(int(raw_result))\n        else:\n            results.append(raw_result)\n    return tuple(results)"}
