{"task_id": "Mbpp/306", "solution": "def max_sum_increasing_subseq(arr, n, i, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence from arr[0...i]\n    that also includes arr[k] (where k > i).\n    \"\"\"\n    # Convert all elements to floats for consistent numeric operations.\n    arr = [float(x) for x in arr]\n\n    # dp[j] stores the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence ending at arr[j]\n    # for elements within the prefix arr[0...i].\n    dp = [arr[j] for j in range(i + 1)]\n\n    # Compute DP table for the prefix up to index i.\n    for j in range(i + 1):\n        for t in range(j):\n            if arr[t] < arr[j]:\n                dp[j] = max(dp[j], dp[t] + arr[j])\n\n    # arr[k] is the element that must be included.\n    val_k = arr[k]\n\n    # Find the maximum sum from dp[j] such that arr[j] can precede arr[k].\n    best_prefix_sum = float('-inf') # Use negative infinity to correctly handle cases where no valid prefix is found.\n\n    for j in range(i + 1):\n        if arr[j] < val_k:\n            best_prefix_sum = max(best_prefix_sum, dp[j])\n\n    # If no valid prefix element was found (i.e., no arr[j] < val_k),\n    # the subsequence is just [arr[k]].\n    if best_prefix_sum == float('-inf'):\n        return val_k\n    else:\n        # Otherwise, combine the best prefix sum with arr[k].\n        return best_prefix_sum + val_k"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/312", "solution": "import math\ndef volume_cone(radius, height):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the volume of a cone using its radius and height.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Formula for the volume of a cone: V = (1/3) * pi * r^2 * h\n    volume = (1/3) * math.pi * (radius ** 2) * height\n    return volume"}
