{"task_id": "Mbpp/428", "solution": "def shell_sort(arr):\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list using the Shell Sort algorithm with Knuth's gap sequence.\n    \"\"\"\n    data = list(arr)  # Create a mutable copy of the input list.\n    n = len(data)\n\n    if n <= 1:\n        return data\n\n    # Generate Knuth's gap sequence (1, 4, 13, 40, ...).\n    # Gaps are collected in ascending order, then reversed for sorting passes.\n    gaps = []\n    current_h = 1\n    while current_h < n:\n        gaps.append(current_h)\n        current_h = 3 * current_h + 1\n    \n    gaps.reverse() # Use gaps in descending order for the sorting passes.\n\n    for gap in gaps:\n        # Perform a gapped insertion sort for the current gap size.\n        for i in range(gap, n):\n            temp = data[i]\n            j = i\n            # Shift elements that are larger than temp to the right.\n            while j >= gap and data[j - gap] > temp:\n                data[j] = data[j - gap]\n                j -= gap\n            # Place temp in its correct position.\n            data[j] = temp\n            \n    return data"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/433", "solution": "def check_greater(arr: list, value: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given value is strictly greater than all elements in the array.\n    An empty array is considered vacuously true.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not arr:\n        return True\n    max_val = max(arr)\n    return value > max_val"}
