{"task_id": "Mbpp/556", "solution": "def find_Odd_Pair(arr: list, n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts pairs of integers in the array whose XOR value is odd.\n    An XOR is odd if one number is even and the other is odd.\n    \"\"\"\n    evens = 0\n    odds = 0\n\n    for num in arr:\n        # Check if the number is even using a bitwise AND operation.\n        if (num & 1) == 0:\n            evens += 1\n        else:\n            odds += 1\n\n    # The total number of pairs (one even, one odd) is the product of their counts.\n    return evens * odds"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/555", "solution": "def difference(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the difference between the sum of cubes of the first n natural numbers\n    and the sum of the first n natural numbers using an O(1) formula.\n    \"\"\"\n    sum_of_n = n * (n + 1) // 2\n    return sum_of_n * (sum_of_n - 1)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/558", "solution": "def digit_distance_nums(a: int, b: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of per-digit absolute differences between two integers.\n    Digits are aligned from the right, and the shorter number is left-padded with zeros.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Convert numbers to lists of their absolute digits.\n    # For example, abs(-123) becomes [1, 2, 3].\n    digits_a = [int(c) for c in str(abs(a))]\n    digits_b = [int(c) for c in str(abs(b))]\n\n    # Pad the shorter digit list with leading zeros to match the length of the longer one.\n    # For example, [1, 2, 3] and [4, 5] would become [1, 2, 3] and [0, 4, 5].\n    max_len = max(len(digits_a), len(digits_b))\n    digits_a = [0] * (max_len - len(digits_a)) + digits_a\n    digits_b = [0] * (max_len - len(digits_b)) + digits_b\n\n    # Calculate the sum of absolute differences for each pair of corresponding digits.\n    # For example, for [1,2,3] and [0,4,5], this sums abs(1-0) + abs(2-4) + abs(3-5).\n    total_distance = sum(abs(d_a - d_b) for d_a, d_b in zip(digits_a, digits_b))\n\n    return total_distance"}
