{"task_id": "Mbpp/564", "solution": "def count_Pairs(numbers, n):\n    # Consider only the first 'n' elements of the input list.\n    effective_sequence = numbers[:n]\n\n    # If there are fewer than two elements, no pairs can be formed.\n    if len(effective_sequence) < 2:\n        return 0\n\n    # Define an inline helper to calculate combinations of 2 items from k.\n    def n_choose_2_inline(k):\n        if k < 2:\n            return 0\n        return k * (k - 1) // 2\n\n    # Count the frequency of each number in the effective sequence.\n    counts = {}\n    for num in effective_sequence:\n        counts[num] = counts.get(num, 0) + 1\n\n    # Calculate the total possible unordered pairs from all elements.\n    total_elements_in_seq = len(effective_sequence)\n    total_possible_pairs = n_choose_2_inline(total_elements_in_seq)\n\n    # Sum the pairs of identical elements (e.g., pairs of '1's if '1' appears multiple times).\n    same_value_pairs = sum(n_choose_2_inline(count) for count in counts.values())\n\n    # The result is the total pairs minus those with equal elements.\n    return total_possible_pairs - same_value_pairs"}
