{"task_id": "Mbpp/635", "solution": "def heap_sort(lst):\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list using the heap sort algorithm.\n    It creates a copy of the input list to perform an in-place sort and returns the sorted copy.\n    \"\"\"\n    arr = list(lst)\n    n = len(arr)\n\n    def _heapify(arr_local, n_local, i_local):\n        \"\"\"\n        Helper function to maintain the max-heap property for a subtree rooted at index i_local.\n        \"\"\"\n        largest = i_local\n        l = 2 * i_local + 1\n        r = 2 * i_local + 2\n\n        if l < n_local and arr_local[l] > arr_local[largest]:\n            largest = l\n\n        if r < n_local and arr_local[r] > arr_local[largest]:\n            largest = r\n\n        if largest != i_local:\n            arr_local[i_local], arr_local[largest] = arr_local[largest], arr_local[i_local]\n            _heapify(arr_local, n_local, largest)\n\n    # Build a max-heap (rearrange array)\n    for i in range(n // 2 - 1, -1, -1):\n        _heapify(arr, n, i)\n\n    # One by one extract elements from heap\n    for i in range(n - 1, 0, -1):\n        arr[0], arr[i] = arr[i], arr[0]  # Move current root to end\n        _heapify(arr, i, 0)  # Call _heapify on the reduced heap\n\n    return arr"}
