{"task_id": "Mbpp/633", "solution": "def pair_xor_Sum(numbers, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of XOR of all unordered pairs of numbers in the given list.\n    This is efficiently computed by iterating through each bit position and summing contributions.\n    \"\"\"\n    list_length = len(numbers)\n    if list_length < 2:\n        return 0\n\n    total_xor_sum = 0\n    # The design context implies a default maximum of 32 bits for the numbers.\n    max_bits = 32\n\n    for bit_pos in range(max_bits):\n        count_ones = 0\n        for num in numbers:\n            # Check if the current bit_pos-th bit is set in the number\n            if (num >> bit_pos) & 1:\n                count_ones += 1\n        \n        # Calculate the number of pairs where this bit position will result in 1\n        # This occurs when one number has the bit set and the other has it cleared.\n        count_zeros = list_length - count_ones\n        pairs_with_bit_set = count_ones * count_zeros\n        \n        # Add the contribution of this bit position to the total sum\n        total_xor_sum += pairs_with_bit_set * (1 << bit_pos)\n        \n    return total_xor_sum"}
